# crypt.manifest — config owned by the disk-encryption subsystem (w-crypt).
#
# Layered (update-system.md phase 3):
#   • /usr/share/w/defaults/crypt.conf   — W's default TPM2 PCR set. Class managed.
#   • /usr/share/w/defaults/crypt.schema — who may set each key (system-scope: a
#     user file must never be able to relax what seals the LUKS unlock key).
#   • /etc/w/crypt.conf — this machine's DEVIATIONS only. Class override: silently
#     restoring the vendor PCR set would break auto-unlock until a re-enroll, so the
#     update never touches it. `w-reset limine` drops the deviations; re-run the
#     relevant `w-crypt` command afterwards to re-seal.
#
# The Limine/LUKS boot bits ship separately (package-limine.md), not tracked here.
#
# Format: <path>\t<class>   class: managed | override
/usr/share/w/defaults/crypt.conf	managed
/usr/share/w/defaults/crypt.schema	managed
/etc/w/crypt.conf	override
